      <description>&lt;div id="storytext" class="storytext storylocation linkLocation"&gt;       &lt;div id="resg-s1-147629" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 3639;         --source-height: 2426;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3639x2426+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fb7%2F15%2F0e8069e84cba8b3b26e07c0b9450%2Fap26283272621777.jpg" class="img" alt="A protester shout slogans as they are detained and taken in a police vehicle during a protest demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026." fetchpriority="high" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 A protester shout slogans as they are detained and taken in a police vehicle during a protest demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Manish Swarup/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;NEW DELHI — Indian authorities deployed a sweeping security crackdown across New Delhi and detained thousands of protesters Saturday as India's youth "Cockroach" movement sought to intensify a nationwide campaign against a contentious voter list revision that has fueled anger at Prime Minister Narendra Modi's Hindu nationalist government and election authorities.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Police moved to break up the demonstration before it could begin, intercepting demonstrators on their way to Jantar Mantar, the designated protest site in the heart of India's capital, chasing off some and detaining many others. Some were dragged away before being bundled into police vehicles and taken to temporary detention centers. Several "Cockroach" movement leaders, opposition lawmakers and student activists were detained before arriving, effectively crippling the protest ahead of its start.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;The crackdown extended beyond the protest venue, with police stopping buses, cars and other vehicles at checkpoints on routes into the capital and searching for demonstrators. Jantar Mantar was barricaded, while anti-riot vehicles equipped with tear gas launchers were stationed along key routes. Restrictions on mobile internet and access to parts of the city added to the hurdles facing protesters.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Police said Friday they had denied permission for the protest because the request was submitted late.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Sambit Patra, a spokesperson for Modi's party, dismissed the demonstrators as "anarchic elements."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147603-100" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESG-S1-147603-100" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"Their flop show has been completely demolished," Patra said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The scale of the crackdown underscored the authorities' determination to disrupt a fast-growing protest campaign that has mobilized thousands of young people, drawn opposition support and intensified scrutiny of Modi. The protests also come at a politically sensitive time, months after demonstrations led by the "Cockroach" movement over exam paper leaks forced Modi's education minister to resign in July.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147630" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 2000;         --source-height: 1333;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/2000x1333+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F6a%2F15%2F4eac9f96465696b9ed5804d964e9%2Fap26283285575285.jpg" class="img" alt="Policemen detain protesters during a youth demonstration demanding the resignation of the country&amp;#039;s election chief Gyanesh Kumar, in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Policemen detain protesters during a youth demonstration demanding the resignation of the country's election chief Gyanesh Kumar, in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Vipin/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;Police detain leaders and tighten grip around protest site&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Leaders of the "Cockroach" movement Abhijeet Dipke, Saurav Das and Ashutosh Ranka, who were expected to be at the forefront of the protest, were detained after arriving at Delhi airport from Mumbai on Saturday. A video shared by the "Cockroach Janta Party" on X showed police boarding the aircraft and detaining the three men.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"The pre-planned interception by Delhi Police aims to cripple the leadership of today's peaceful demonstrations before they even reach the protest site," the movement said in a statement.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147603-101" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESG-S1-147603-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Loudspeakers around the protest site warned that gatherings of five or more people were banned in parts of New Delhi, as authorities imposed sweeping security restrictions rarely seen in the capital. Journalists also faced restrictions in some areas, with police briefly detaining some of them.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Some protesters nevertheless broke through police cordons, chanting slogans against Modi and election authorities before being detained.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"We are a democracy, yet peaceful protests are being crushed by force. Shouldn't we fight for our rights," said Tanya Negi, a college student who traveled from Mumbai with two friends and arrived early Saturday. "Why is Modi afraid of India's young people?"&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The police response marked an extraordinary show of force in a capital where Modi's government has repeatedly sought to contain public dissent in the past. Under Modi, authorities have often used arrests and restrictions on public gatherings to contain demonstrations, raising questions about the space for protests in the world's largest democracy.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The latest crackdown renewed criticism from opposition leaders, who accused the government of curbing dissent.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"Is there a democracy in this country? A total siege over the city. Citizens are being driven out," opposition lawmaker John Brittas told The Associated Press. Brittas was later detained by police.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147631" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 4110;         --source-height: 2740;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg 1800w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1025px) 650px, calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/4110x2740+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F32%2F76%2Fb174907e4529ac0fde6e9085a3d7%2Fap26283372191054.jpg" class="img" alt="Security personnel detain a protester during a demonstration by the Cockroach Janta Party demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Security personnel detain a protester during a demonstration by the Cockroach Janta Party demanding the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar in New Delhi, India, Saturday, Oct. 10, 2026.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          Manish Swarup/AP                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;button class="toggle-caption" aria-label=""&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;abbr title="Toggle Caption" class="toggle-caption__info"&gt;i&lt;/abbr&gt;              &lt;/button&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;India's voter list dispute raises election fairness concerns&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The protests center on India's Election Commission's Special Intensive Revision, which the opposition says has disenfranchised millions of eligible voters. Protesters demand the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar and an end to the change, which has removed more than 130 million names from voter lists so far.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The Election Commission and the government reject allegations of voter manipulation, saying the revision is intended to eliminate duplicate and ineligible entries.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;The dispute has become a rallying point for opposition parties seeking to challenge Modi's Hindu nationalist Bharatiya Janata Party.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Saturday's planned demonstration follows days of protests in the Indian capital where opposition lawmakers also stepped up their campaign, with Congress party leader Rahul Gandhi being briefly detained by police.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-147603-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESG-S1-147603-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Gandhi and other opposition leaders have accused the commission of conducting the voter revision in a way that benefits Modi's party. The opposition says voters more likely to support its parties have been disproportionately affected by the removals, while supporters of the BJP have been spared or added to the lists.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The commission and the government deny the allegations.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;India's youth movement broadens campaign against Modi&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For the "Cockroach" movement, the voter list dispute offers an opportunity to broaden its campaign.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The movement began online in May and gained prominence through demonstrations, sit-ins and hunger strikes over alleged exam paper leaks. Those protests culminated in the resignation of Modi's education minister in July, a rare political setback for a prime minister who has maintained a firm hold on national power for more than 12 years.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;For Modi, the protests pose a challenge midway through his third term, though their political impact remains unclear. National elections are not due until 2029, but state elections next year in BJP-ruled Uttar Pradesh, India's most populous state, and Gujarat, Modi's home state, will test the party's standing.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
